<odoo noupdate="1">

  <!-- ==================================================================
       WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE
       ==================================================================
       No ir.model.access row and no ir.rule for hr.shift.planning or
       hr.overtime.request. Both are officer models with no base.group_user
       ACL (pb_hr_workforce/security/ir.model.access.csv), and P8 keeps it
       that way: the portal reads them SUDO, scoped to the employee the
       facade resolved from the session, so the widening is one employee
       wide and lasts one request. Adding an ACL row would open the model
       to every internal user and then rely on a record rule to close it
       again — strictly more surface for strictly no gain, since no ESS
       page reads those models through a generic ORM call.

       No new rule for hr.attendance.correction either: pb_attendance_flow
       already ships `correction_rule_user_own_and_reports` (own + direct
       reports) for base.group_user, with the matching ACL row. The portal
       creates through it AS THE REAL USER and the model's own create path
       is what stamps create_uid. What P8 adds is the target FORCING, and
       that lives in pb.ess.workforce.request_fix, not in a rule — a rule
       can only refuse a bad value, it cannot decide what the right one is
       (I-H3).
       ================================================================== -->

  <!-- The employee's own shift acknowledgment lives on hr.shift.planning
       and is written only through the sentinel (see shift_planning_ack.py).
       There is no group that may write it, on purpose. -->

</odoo>
